{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.WenzlLevelStratum","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.WenzlLevelStratum","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Field.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.List.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.List.Basic"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.principalSpec_numerator_eq_zero_of_lt_length","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.principalSpec_numerator_eq_zero_of_lt_length","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/WenzlLevelStratum.lean#L98-L111","doc":"**Level-integer vanishing law, algebraic half.**\nAt integer level `k`, the principal-specialisation numerator\n`∏_{x ∈ λ} (1 - Q^(k + c(x)))` vanishes for every partition with strictly more than\n`k` rows — for *any* `Q` in *any* field, including `Q = 0`.\n\nThis is the exact statement that generates the level-integer ladder: raising the\nlevel past `k` is what re-admits the `(k+1)`-row stratum. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.neg_mem_partitionContents_of_lt_length","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.neg_mem_partitionContents_of_lt_length","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/WenzlLevelStratum.lean#L86-L96","doc":"**Level-integer vanishing law, combinatorial half.**\nA partition with strictly more than `k` rows — all rows nonempty — has a cell of\ncontent `-k`, namely the first cell of row `k`.\n\nThe positivity hypothesis is essential, not decorative: for `lam = [3, 0]` and\n`k = 1`, row `1` is empty and `-1` is *not* a content (checked below). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.neg_mem_contentsFrom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.neg_mem_contentsFrom","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/WenzlLevelStratum.lean#L56-L84","doc":"**Level-integer vanishing law, combinatorial half (indexed form).**\nIf every row of `lam` is nonempty, then row `k` of the block starting at index `i`\nsupplies a cell of content `-(i + k)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.partitionContents","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.partitionContents","kind":"def","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/WenzlLevelStratum.lean#L53-L54","doc":"Contents of a partition presented as its list of row lengths. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.contentsFrom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.contentsFrom","kind":"def","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/WenzlLevelStratum.lean#L45-L51","doc":"Contents `c(i,j) = j - i` of the cells of the rows `lam`, where the first row of\n`lam` is row index `i`.  A row of length `len` contributes `len` cells with contents\n`0 - i, 1 - i, …, (len-1) - i`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}